  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Báciga. Type: Fishing (Spanish Deck). Rules: Capture cards summing to 15. Sota=8, Cab=9, Rey=10. Scoring: Escobas, Coins, 7-of-Coins, Cartas, Setenta. Declarations: Flor, Escalera, Báciga, Chorizo. Target: 21.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Báciga! The table is set with four cards. Before you play your first card, do you have a declaration? A Flor, a Báciga, or maybe the legendary Chorizo? Speak now, then take your turn to find a 15-sum.',
    objective: 'Be the first to reach 21 points through captures and hand declarations.',
    gameplay: '1. Dealer gives 3 cards to each player, 4 face-up on table. 2. Declaration phase: players may announce Chorizo, Flor, Báciga, or Escalera before play. 3. In turn, each player plays one card to capture table cards that sum to 15, or adds a card to the table. 4. Escoba: capturing all table cards scores bonus. 5. When hands empty, dealer deals 3 more cards; repeat until deck exhausted. 6. Score: Oros (coins), Cartas (cards), Setenta (sevens). First to 21 wins.',
    keyRules: [
      '21 points wins the game.',
      'The 7 of Coins is the most valuable individual card.',
      'If the initial 4 cards on the table sum to 15 or 30, the Dealer takes them as 1 or 2 Escobas immediately.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2-4 players. 4-player games are usually partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
      deck: '40-card Spanish deck (1-7, 10-12). Note: 10 (Sota), 11 (Caballo), 12 (Rey).',
      equipment: 'Standard Spanish deck, pen and paper for 21-point tracking.',
      dealing: '1. Dealer deals 3 cards to each player face down. 2. 4 cards are dealt face up to the table. 3. Dealing is counter-clockwise.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Dealer gives 3 cards to each player, 4 face-up on table. 2. Declaration phase: players may announce Chorizo, Flor, Báciga, or Escalera before play. 3. In turn, each player plays one card to capture table cards that sum to 15, or adds a card to the table. 4. Escoba: capturing all table cards scores bonus. 5. When hands empty, dealer deals 3 more cards; repeat until deck exhausted. 6. Score: Oros (coins), Cartas (cards), Setenta (sevens). First to 21 wins.',
